      "notes": "1. The UF Honors Program’s mission is to connect, nurture and engage the next generation of scholars who change the world. How do you envision yourself contributing to this mission? Consider the people, experiences, resources, and aspirations that have shaped your journey thus far and your future plans. (400 words)2. The Innovation Academy (IA) at UF is a groundbreaking academic program that pulls unique students from more than 25 majors into a spring-summer academic calendar filled with energy, collisions that become ideas, and one common minor: Innovation. The Innovation Academy is one of the nation's most forward-looking undergraduate programs at one of its most dynamic research universities. Innovation Academy gives motivated students a small-college experience focused on innovation, creativity, entrepreneurship, ethics and leadership on a unique spring-summer schedule. The IA enrolls and supports academically talented students focused on developing knowledge to grow new business opportunities, services and products through curricular and co-curricular experiences. Discuss why you are interested in becoming a UF Innovation Academy student and how it will influence your professional career path. Please use a maximum of 300 words in your essay for full consideration.3. Please provide more details on your most meaningful commitment outside of the classroom while in high school and explain why it was meaningful. This could be related to an extracurricular activity, work, volunteering, an academic activity, family responsibility, or any other non-classroom activity. https://admissions.ufl.edu/cost-and-aid/residency#fee-waiver",
